# CQ 17: Which entities provide no service?
#
# Clause 5.2.2 has an entity of one layer provide a service to the layer above
# it. An entity providing none is either the topmost of a stack, where there is
# no layer above to serve, or a gap in the description.
#
# The layer is reported alongside for that reason. An application entity
# providing no service is ordinary, and a network entity providing none is
# usually unfinished, and the answer alone cannot tell the two apart.
#
# OWL cannot require the service under the open world assumption: an entity
# without one is unstated rather than serviceless. The answer therefore reports
# where a model has stayed silent, and SHACL is where it would become a rule.
PREFIX iso7498: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498#>
SELECT ?entity ?layerNumber ?subsystem
WHERE {
  ?entity a iso7498:Entity .
  OPTIONAL { ?subsystem iso7498:hasEntity ?entity ;
                        iso7498:atLayer/iso7498:layerNumber ?layerNumber }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?entity iso7498:providesService ?any }
} ORDER BY DESC(?layerNumber) ?entity
